    "blurb": "Features a blistering Dark Star, an incendiary The Other One, and a powerful Alligator > Drums > Caution sequence. Jerry's guitar tone is pristine while Phil’s bass shines on the improvisations. Soundboard recordings capture the band in top form.",
    "review": "The Electric Factory show of February 15, 1969 finds the Dead firing on all cylinders. Set 1 launches from a tight Doin' That Rag into an incendiary The Other One, then drifts through a mellow Morning Dew before rolling into a seamless Dupree's Diamond Blues → Mountains Of The Moon → Dark Star suite that showcases Jerry Garcia’s crystalline lead and Phil Lesh’s warm, intricate bass work. Set 2 ratchets up the intensity with a thunderous Alligator → Drums → Alligator → Caution jam that pushes the rhythm section into a locked‑in phase, while Cosmic Charlie adds a bright, melodic lift. Highlights like Dark Star, The Other One and Mountains Of The Moon are captured on an excellent soundboard tape that balances instrument separation and dynamics, making this one of the era’s most compelling high‑energy performances.",
